list.item:
All pediatric patients younger than 6 years of age

   [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2, 5.3), Use in Specific Populations (8.4)
                        ].

Significant respiratory depression

   [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2)
                        ].

Acute or severe bronchial asthma in an unmonitored setting or in the absence of resuscitative equipment

   [see Warnings and Precautions (5.4)
                        ].

Known or suspected gastrointestinal obstruction, including paralytic ileus

   [see Warnings and Precautions (5.9)
                        ].

Hypersensitivity to hydrocodone, homatropine, or any of the inactive ingredients in hydrocodone bitartrate and homatropine methylbromide

   [see Adverse Reactions (6)
                        ].
